          "path": "_m/w/e/c/p/kowloon-walled-city-park-wp/japanese-street-fashion-in-the.jpg",
          "filename": "Japanese Street Fashion in the Kowloon Walled City (6816387287).jpg",
          "caption": "The Kowloon Walled City was a largely ungoverned densely populated den located in Kowloon, Hong Kong. When the New Territories were leased to the British in 1898 the city became a Chinese enclave. A population surge and inadequate policing led to the city becoming a den of prostitution, drug use and gambling.\nEviction and demolition of the city began in 1993 and two years later the Kowloon Walled City Park opened in its place.\n\nHere a young woman dressed in a Japanese street fashion type poses for a photographer within the park boundaries.",
          "alt": "The Kowloon Walled City was a largely ungoverned densely populated den located in Kowloon, Hong Kong. When the New Territories were leased to the British in 1898 the city became a Chinese enclave. A population surge and inadequate policing led to the city becoming a den of prostitution, drug use and gambling.\nEviction and demolition of the city began in 1993 and two years later the Kowloon Walled City Park opened in its place.\n\nHere a young woman dressed in a Japanese street fashion type poses for a photographer within the park boundaries.",
